// What `npm run typecheck` actually checks: the app that ships.
//
// WHY NOT JUST `tsc -p tsconfig.json`. That reports 277 errors today and would
// be red from the day it was added. A gate that is always red is worth exactly
// as much as one that is always green — which is the lesson `npm run lint`
// taught here: the script existed, had no config, failed every time, and so
// nobody ran it and nothing was ever linted.
//
// The excluded 277 are NOT app defects and are NOT dismissed:
//   * ~222 in *.stories.tsx — Storybook 8 moved `Meta`/`StoryObj` to the
//     renderer package `@storybook/react`, which is not installed here. A
//     dependency question, not a type error in our code.
//   * ~55 in __tests__ — real looseness in test code (unsafe casts, fixtures
//     missing required props). Worth fixing, on its own pass.
//
// Both are tracked work. Narrow the exclusions as they are cleared; do not
// widen them to make a build pass.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "**/*.stories.ts",
    "**/*.stories.tsx",
    "**/__tests__/**",
    "**/__mocks__/**"
  ]
}
